WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a fantastic film.
-Thank you.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You play --This is based on -
a, reporter actually wrote

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very famous profile
of Mr. Rogers.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He did.
-And he's is a bit cynical

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And sort of discovers

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot about Mr. Rogers
over the process.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You grew up in Wales.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you have any context
for Mr. Rogers?

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. So, ironically,
I'm very cynical

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I knew nothing
about Mr. Rogers.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.487 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It was perfect casting.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you got to
take the same journey.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.890 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yes. I did very little.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was it like,
the first time?

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause, I imagine
it must be very jarring

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're told
about Mr. Rogers

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you go back
and watch Mr. Rogers.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your first reaction
-Well, my first reaction,

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.602
I read the script and said
to Keri, "Who is Mr. Rogers?

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:40.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's, like "Get out. Get out.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she pointed up.
Mr. Rogers's voice, as it will

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:47.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
is already in our living roo
'cause our 2 1/2-year-old

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
was watching
"Daniel Tiger's Neighborhood."

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I was, like,
"Oh, right, yeah."

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:53.720
So, then I took a deep div
and I thought something's wrong,

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.955 size:84% position:42%
because this gentleman
is speaking very slowly

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it seemingly
only had one camera

00:00:57.257 --> 00:01:00.860
that they would never cut away
and was he forgetting his line

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I realized
it wasn't for me.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was for children
of a certain age.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.267
Then, I discovered
the true genius of "Mr. Rogers."

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, absolutely.
They do say,

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you get introduced
to Mr. Rogers,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's better if it happens
when you're young.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not, like "The Sopranos,
where they're like,

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, you got to rewatch it."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.212 line:92%
-"Start from the beginning."

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Can't come in the middle
on 'Mr. Rogers.'"

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no.
What were your --

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:25.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was kids' television like
for you, growing up?

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A little strange.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
my first language is Welsh

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, at that time,
when I was growing up,

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Welsh-language station
was a fledgling,

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
was discovering, you know,
its identity.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:38.631 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It wasn't quite sure

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:41.201
what children's television
should be or wanted to be.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.937
A lot of strange puppets.
There were two gentlemen

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
who kind of would put a jacket
over the camera

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then beat each other up.
-Okay.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was -- It was strange.
So I went into acting.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very strange
to do children's televisio

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
where part of it is
they hide themselves

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the children.
-And then -- Yes.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then beat each other up.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:02.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, that's what we did,
as children in Wales.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did your --
Is your 3-year-old --

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, you said
he was watching "Daniel Tiger.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:08.962
Did you start watching "Mr
Rogers" with him, as well?

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.798 size:84% position:42%
-Sadly, or not, I think
he'll be richer for it,

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:14.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he kind of became
my Mr. Rogers guinea pig.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, then I went and
put him in front of the show -

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
the actual show --
back, you know,

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:24.277
the black-and-white version, and
it was an incredible moment.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He went for it?
-Oh, he still is.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.515 size:78% position:39%
It's, like, his daily
30-minute meditation.

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.717 size:88% position:44%
-Oh, that's fantastic.
It is really meditative.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that's the great thing
about Mr. Rogers.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:35.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And also as a parent,
I learned far more

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:36.289 size:88% position:44% line:92%
from those 30 minutes...

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:39.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I'm the one
behind him, going...

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:44.664 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So we're both learning.
-Good.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.501
'Cause, I remember you wer
terrible at putting on a sweater

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.203 size:78% position:39%
last time I saw you,
and now from watching

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.739
"Mr. Rogers," you just get i
on and off, like, right away

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, like nobody's business.
Yeah.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was -- Listen,
as well you know,

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:59.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was no stranger
to a wool knit sweater.

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:02.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
Six years, I served my time.
-That's right.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
You -- Tom Hanks obviously
plays Mr. Rogers.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.687
And you know, one of the thing
we all know about Mr. Rogers i

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the things
we all know about Tom Hanks,

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.558 size:81% position:41%
which is he's actually
as lovely as he seems.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's kind of crazy, though
right?

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I'm almost to the poin
of going,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:19.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
"When do I start a new rumor
just saying

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.067
that I'm gonna take down Hanks?"
-Yeah.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:24.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just, like full-time bad guy
-I'll do both.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.840
I'll take down Rogers and Hanks.
I'll go, "Listen,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've discovered
two things about them.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.511
You're not gonna like it.
Listen to me, America."

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:34.447
-Yeah, "They both have
a very dirty, dark secret

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is the same thing,
and it's awful."

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
It's to do with a cardigan

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you get...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:43.356
The first time you do a scen
with somebody like Tom Hanks

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.959
do you feel like, does it
make it harder as an actor

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.461 size:84% position:42%
because you are aware,
obviously, as a person,

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.231 size:81% position:41%
that it's Tom Hanks.
-Well, listen, for me,

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:54.167
not knowing Mr. Rogers, To
Hanks was my Mr. Rogers.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:58.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
I grew up with Tom Hanks.
So it took me days

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:02.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
of trying to act
as if I wasn't nervous

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.611 line:92%
or perversely star-struck

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:07.347 size:81% position:41%
before I could start
acting with Tom Hanks.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:08.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, I was acting,

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:12.252
trying to be calm and trying
to stop my head from sweatin

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.086 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in front of Tom Hanks

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
before I could do anything
to do with the film.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it was one of the greate
acting jobs,

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:20.193
I think, I've ever done.
-Well, we all tip our caps

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ah, yes.
-So, you had done this before.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:26.032
So, Keri, your costar and
partner now in real life,

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:29.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, your first two years
in "The Americans,"

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:30.703 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I have heard it told

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:31.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were doing
the same thing with her.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were not acting
to be in the scene.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.174 size:81% position:41%
You were just trying
to, like, impress her.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The very same thing.
So, I spent the first two year

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "The Americans"
trying to impress Keri.

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:43.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm quite sure
my acting was at its worst

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And the same with Tom Hanks.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wasn't acting
to serve the script.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was trying
to impress Tom Hanks.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:52.892
So, I'm just in this cycle
of trying to impress peopl

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not really
serving the script.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That's the key, though.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
As long as your --
As long as your shows

00:04:58.798 --> 00:04:59.699 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
run enough seasons,

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:00.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
we eventually get to see
you, the actor.

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:03.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Eventually, if you
give me the real estate,

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:04.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll get there.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:08.141
I just need a solid three years.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:11.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have not seen you
since "The Americans" ended --

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
a show, I've told you before
I love so much.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:16.416 size:75% position:38%
It must be wonderful
to have left a thing

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:19.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
in very, just a pristine endin
of a show

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I think is going to endur
for years.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does it feel great?
-Incredible.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know,
we were all very well.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'd had
this incredible five years

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:30.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were all very worried
as to how -- what would happen

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:33.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, in all fairnes
to the writers,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
they ended it
beautifully and perfectly.

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:38.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think-- I don't feel
we wrung the towel dry.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
We kind of left it
on the right note.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was great.
Keri and you --

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.178 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you have a 3-year-old,

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is very exciting
for a 3-year-old.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's is going to be
in the new "Star Wars" film.

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:51.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, as soon as he
grasps that concept.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:52.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because all you have right no
to show him

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
is her outfit in the film.
-Yes.

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this has been released.
-That's been released.

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.426 line:92%
Well, what actually happened is,

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:04.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't even know
who the toymaker is,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:07.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they very kindly sent
the bobblehead to our house.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:08.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure, that's
a nice thing to do.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:11.571
-Yes, so, obviously, it's
not very well-proportioned

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
The head is giant.
it's a bobblehead.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.875 line:92%
And he opened it with Keri

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:19.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
Keri tried to explain
what this bobblehead was.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then she -- I came hom
and he ran up to me

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:26.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the bobblehead
and said, "Mom's inside."

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.453 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went, "Good.
Keep her there."

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:32.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"It'll be our secret."

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-"Don't let her out."

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.428 size:78% position:39%
-"Don't let her out."
Every now and then,

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:38.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mom needs to be
in the bobblehead.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:41.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's always such a pleasur
to see you.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:45.037 size:84% position:42%
Congrats on the film.
Matthew Rhys everybody.

